+# Dependency queue (experimental, Switch 2 titles): compute dispatches and DMA copies whose output
+# the CPU reads or that write GPU-written command lists are counted per frame (log every 600
+# frames), the device opens a second queue (compute-only family, else a second graphics queue)
+# and the scheduler a second command stream for them. Later stages route them there so the
+# CPU-side waits no longer drain the whole graphics queue. Off: nothing changes.
+#EDEN_NX2_ASYNC_DEP_QUEUE=1
+
 
 
 #EDEN_NX2_MME_JIT=0
